IronsDeploy

A lightweight deployment orchestrator for self-hosted and local network environments. IronsDeploy sits between raw Docker Compose and heavyweight solutions like Kubernetes, providing version tracking, health monitoring, and atomic rollbacks.

🚀 Status: Early Development

This project is currently being implemented in Go. We are moving from the design phase to the MVP (Phase 1).

🛠 Tech Stack

Language: Go 1.22+

CLI Framework: Cobra & Viper

Container Engine: Docker SDK (Moby)

State Management: SQLite

Config Format: YAML

📂 Project Structure

We follow the standard Go project layout:

cmd/ironsdeploy: Entry point for the CLI binary.

internal/cli: Command definitions and flag parsing.

internal/config: YAML parsing and validation logic.

internal/core: The orchestration engine and deployment logic.

internal/docker: Wrappers for the Docker Engine API.

internal/state: SQLite persistence for deployment history and rollbacks.

✨ Core Features (MVP)

[ ] Config-driven deployments: Define your stack in ironsdeploy.yaml.

[ ] Version tracking: Automatic tagging of deployments.

[ ] Health checks: Built-in monitoring with configurable endpoints.

[ ] Atomic Rollbacks: One-command revert to previous stable states.

[ ] Multi-environment: Native support for local, staging, and production overrides.

🏁 Getting Started

Prerequisites

Go installed.

Docker running locally.

Development Setup

Clone the repository.

Install dependencies:

go mod download


Run the CLI:

go run cmd/ironsdeploy/main.go --help


